== a new login, logged in at its end
Claude Code logs in with its own login, in a session on box:

    claude auth login

It runs in the session login-claude (box/fake2). Answer it there, or press ctrl+\ to leave it running.

  ✓ Claude Code      /home/dev/.local/bin/claude, logged in (`claude auth status` says so)
-> attached to fake2
== a new login, left by a detach
Claude Code logs in with its own login, in a session on box:

    claude auth login

It runs in the session login-claude (box/fake2). Answer it there, or press ctrl+\ to leave it running.

  ! Claude Code      /home/dev/.local/bin/claude, not logged in (`claude auth status` says not)

The login keeps running. Attach again: <name> attach --id -- box/fake2
-> attached to fake2
== a login that runs
The login of Claude Code already runs in box/s2. Attaching to it. Answer it there, or press ctrl+\ to leave it running.

  ! Claude Code      /home/dev/.local/bin/claude, not logged in (`claude auth status` says not)

The login keeps running. Attach again: <name> attach --id -- box/s2
-> attached to s2
== input off
Started box/fake2. Attach to finish the login: <name> attach --id -- box/fake2
== input off, a login that runs
The login of Claude Code already runs in box/s2. Attach to finish the login: <name> attach --id -- box/s2
== input off, two logins that run
The login of Claude Code already runs in box/s3. Attach to finish the login: <name> attach --id -- box/s3
